Body:
> Agree, the 1m context did worked very well, if it can be brought back, would be awesome, if it is abused and uses too many resources, maybe you guys could create a new tier account, like a donator account, that if an account donated for example 50$ it can use extra content not available to free tier, one time fee or something no subscription base, at least this can generate some revenue, that otherwise will be 0 because people will stuck to free models. Daily limits are ok, but the 1m context made a difference in quality.
> 
> Many are wiling to cintribute to what we believe is a good product and fair offer.

you can solve this for now by adding this to `.config/opencode/opencode.json` : 
```
  "provider": {
    "opencode": {
      "models": {
        "deepseek-v4-flash-free": {
          "limit": {
            "context": 1048576,
            "output": 384000
          }
        }
      }
    },
  }
```

@kitlangton @jlongster @nexxeln  
happy to follow up with progress forwarding to the TUI as a separate feature, wanted to check if that's something the team would want before building it. 
lmk if a design discussion would be useful.
